# Project: Jarvis — Internal Operations Dashboard for Inteck

## Overview
Jarvis is a single-user internal dashboard for the owner of Inteck, a
software development company. Each morning it shows each client's
infrastructure health, deployments, today's tasks, and GitHub activity.
It also generates branded monthly client reports (web link + PDF).
Internal views show full technical detail; client reports show a
curated, client-friendly subset.

## Current Focus: Pilot Client "IDS" (Industrial Door Systems)
- Build and test end-to-end for ONE client: IDS.
- Architecture must support many clients, providers, environments and
  GitHub orgs from day one. Do NOT hardcode IDS in application logic;
  IDS exists only as data (seed script / UI).
- The dashboard must look good with a single client.

### IDS setup (all accounts owned by Inteck)
Environments: PRODUCTION and DEVELOPMENT (development = "staging").

| Resource            | Provider         | Prod | Dev | Repo                          |
|---------------------|------------------|------|-----|-------------------------------|
| workforce-api       | DO App Platform  | yes  | yes | ids.workforce-api             |
| html-pdf-api        | DO App Platform  | yes  | yes | ids.simplx-html-pdf-converter |
| Database            | Supabase         | yes  | yes | —                             |
| Edge functions      | Supabase         | yes  | yes | ids.simplx-serverless         |
| Web UI              | Vercel           | yes  | yes | ids-simplx.ui                 |
| Mobile app (Expo)   | Expo / EAS       | —    | —   | ids-simplx.mobile             |

- DigitalOcean: all 4 APIs run on App Platform. Production and
  development are SEPARATE apps (4 apps total), each imported as its
  own Resource with its own environment. Build DO_APP first; keep
  DO_DROPLET in the design for future clients.
- GitHub org: industrial-door-systems
- Branch mapping: main -> PRODUCTION, pre-production -> DEVELOPMENT
  (configurable per repository). Mobile releases are manual and not
  branch-based.
- APIs may not have /health endpoints yet; fall back to base URL checks.

## Tech Stack
- Monorepo: pnpm workspaces + Turborepo
  - apps/web: Next.js 15 (App Router, TypeScript, Server Components)
  - apps/api: Node.js + Fastify (TypeScript) — integrations, scheduled
    jobs, metric collection, report aggregation, PDF generation,
    credential encryption
  - packages/db: Prisma schema + client (Jarvis's own Supabase Postgres
    project, separate from client databases)
  - packages/shared: shared types, zod schemas, utils
- Auth: Supabase Auth, single user; only ALLOWED_EMAIL may sign in.
  Next.js middleware protects all routes except public report links.
  apps/api verifies the Supabase JWT on every request.
- Jobs: pg-boss (Postgres-backed, no Redis) inside apps/api
- UI: Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui, Recharts
- PDF: Puppeteer in apps/api renders the web report page
- AI: Vercel AI SDK, provider-agnostic, small/cheap model by default,
  behind AI_ENABLED (default false)

## Design: "Jarvis" Look and Feel
- Dark only: near-black background, cyan/electric-blue accents, soft glow
- HUD style: thin glowing borders, subtle grid background, monospace for
  numbers, circular gauges (CPU/memory/disk), sparklines for trends
- Status colours: green healthy, amber warning, red critical, grey
  no data / connection error. "N/A" (e.g. disk on App Platform) is
  neutral, never an error.
- Header: "Good morning. Here's your briefing." + date/time (Europe/London)
- Subtle animation only. Desktop first, usable on mobile.
- Default thresholds: warning >= 75%, critical >= 90% (configurable)
- Restarts: any restart in the last 24h on a PRODUCTION component =
  amber; 3+ in 24h = red.
- Failed latest production deployment = red; health check down = red.
- PRODUCTION drives the client's RAG status. DEVELOPMENT is shown
  separately, visually quieter (collapsed section / muted styling), and
  never turns a client red on its own.

## Data Models
- Client: id, name, slug, logoUrl, contactName, contactEmail, notes,
  active, createdAt
- ProviderAccount: id, clientId (nullable = Inteck-owned), label,
  provider (DIGITALOCEAN | AWS | SUPABASE | VERCEL | EXPO),
  authType (ENV_TOKEN | ENCRYPTED_TOKEN | AWS_ASSUME_ROLE |
  AWS_ACCESS_KEY), encryptedCredentials?, envVarName?, awsRoleArn?,
  awsExternalId?, lastVerifiedAt?, lastError?
  (Inteck-owned accounts use ENV_TOKEN referencing an env var;
  client-owned accounts later use encrypted credentials.)
- Resource: id, clientId, providerAccountId, name,
  environment (PRODUCTION | DEVELOPMENT | NONE),
  type (DO_APP | DO_DROPLET | SUPABASE_PROJECT | SUPABASE_FUNCTIONS |
  VERCEL_PROJECT | EXPO_APP | AWS_EC2),
  externalId (DO app ID / droplet ID / Supabase project ref /
  Vercel project ID / Expo project ID), region?, liveUrl?,
  healthCheckUrl?, repositoryId?,
  config (JSON, e.g. DO componentName, bundleId, iosAppId,
  androidPackage), encryptedSecrets? (e.g. Supabase service role key),
  lastError?, active
- MetricSnapshot: id, resourceId, cpuPercent?, memoryPercent?,
  diskPercent?, restartCount?, dbConnections?, dbSizeBytes?,
  capturedAt (index resourceId + capturedAt)
- MetricRollupHourly: id, resourceId, hour, avg/max for cpu, memory,
  disk, sum restarts, max dbSizeBytes (used by reports)
- HealthCheck: id, resourceId, isUp, statusCode?, responseMs?,
  checkedAt
- Deployment: id, resourceId, externalId, status (BUILDING | SUCCESS |
  FAILED | CANCELED), cause?, commitSha?, commitMessage?, branch?,
  url?, startedAt, finishedAt?  (unique on resourceId + externalId)
- MobileBuild: id, resourceId, externalId, platform (IOS | ANDROID),
  profile, status, appVersion, buildNumber, commitSha?,
  submittedToStore (bool), createdAt, completedAt?
- StoreVersion: id, resourceId, platform, version, releasedAt?,
  checkedAt
- FunctionStats: id, resourceId, periodStart, periodEnd, invocations,
  errors
- Repository: id, clientId, owner, name, productionBranch (default
  "main"), developmentBranch? (e.g. "pre-production"), active
- Task: id, clientId (nullable = internal), title, dueDate, completed,
  completedAt?, createdAt
  (keep simple: no priorities, statuses, assignees or subtasks)
- Report: id, clientId, month (YYYY-MM), data (JSON snapshot),
  summary (text), hiddenSections (string[]), status (DRAFT |
  PUBLISHED), publicToken (random, unguessable), pdfUrl?, createdAt,
  publishedAt?

## Integrations (apps/api, adapter pattern)
Interfaces per capability, e.g.:
  interface MetricsProvider { testConnection(); getMetrics(resource, from, to) }
  interface DeploymentProvider { listDeployments(resource, since) }
  interface DiscoveryProvider { listResources(account) }
One failing provider/resource must never block others; record lastError
and show a warning badge.

### DigitalOcean (DO_API_TOKEN, read scope)
- DO_APP (build first):
  - Discovery: GET /v2/apps — list all apps so the user can import each
    one as a Resource, assign PRODUCTION / DEVELOPMENT, and link a
    repository. Each environment is a separate app. Suggest the
    environment from the app name (e.g. "-dev", "-staging",
    "-preprod") and the deployed branch, but let the user confirm.
  - Store the primary service component name in Resource.config
    (an app may contain several components; default to the first
    service).
  - Metrics per app component via the Monitoring API:
    /v2/monitoring/metrics/apps/cpu_percentage,
    /v2/monitoring/metrics/apps/memory_percentage,
    /v2/monitoring/metrics/apps/restart_count
    (params: app_id, app_component, start, end).
  - Deployments: GET /v2/apps/{id}/deployments — phase, cause, commit
    sha, branch, created/updated times. Map phases to
    BUILDING | SUCCESS | FAILED | CANCELED.
  - liveUrl from the app's live_url; default healthCheckUrl to
    {live_url}/health, falling back to live_url.
  - Disk: not applicable, so store null and show "N/A".
- DO_DROPLET (later): Monitoring API for CPU, memory, disk (needs agent).

### Supabase (SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN — Management API)
- Discovery: list projects so the user can import the IDS prod and dev
  projects and assign environments.
- Project info: plan, region, status, database size.
- DB metrics (CPU, memory, disk, connections): per-project privileged
  metrics endpoint (Prometheus format) authenticated with that
  project's service role key (stored in Resource.encryptedSecrets).
  Parse only the metrics we need.
- Edge functions: list functions with versions and updated dates;
  invocation and error counts via Management API analytics where
  available. If unavailable, degrade gracefully (show N/A).

### Vercel (VERCEL_TOKEN, optional VERCEL_TEAM_ID)
- Discovery: list projects to import.
- Deployments per project: state, target (production / preview),
  commit sha/message, branch, url, created/ready times. Map the
  pre-production branch deployments to DEVELOPMENT.

### Expo / EAS (EXPO_TOKEN)
- Expo GraphQL API: EAS builds (platform, profile, status, version,
  build number, commit) and submissions.
- iOS App Store live version: public iTunes lookup API by bundleId.
- Google Play live version: phase 2 (Google Play Developer API with
  service account). Until then, show latest submitted Android build.

### Health checks
- Every 1 minute for each resource with a healthCheckUrl (default
  /health, fall back to base URL). Record status and response time.
  Uptime % calculated from HealthCheck rows.

### GitHub (GITHUB_TOKEN, classic PAT: repo, read:org)
- Octokit, multiple orgs; searchable repo picker across all orgs.
- Dashboard: commits and PRs from the last 24–48h per client.
- Release tracking using branch mapping:
  - "Released to production": PRs merged into productionBranch.
  - "On staging, awaiting production": commits/PRs in
    developmentBranch not yet in productionBranch (compare API:
    productionBranch...developmentBranch).
- Handle pagination and rate limits; cache briefly.

### AWS (build later, keep in design)
- STS AssumeRole with External ID, or encrypted keys; CloudWatch
  CPUUtilization plus CWAgent mem_used_percent/disk_used_percent.

### Scheduling (pg-boss)
- Metrics: every 5 min. Health checks: every 1 min.
  Deployments/builds: every 5 min. Store versions: every 6 hours.
  GitHub: on demand with caching + hourly sync.
- Hourly rollup job builds MetricRollupHourly.
- Retention: raw metrics and health checks older than 90 days purged
  daily; hourly rollups kept 13 months for reports.

### Credentials
- Inteck-owned tokens come from env vars. Any stored secrets are
  AES-256-GCM encrypted with ENCRYPTION_KEY and decrypted ONLY in
  apps/api. Never send secrets to apps/web or the browser; UI shows
  masked values only. Never log secrets.

## Features (build in order, one step at a time, stop after each)
1. Scaffold monorepo, Prisma schema, Supabase connection, auth,
   Jarvis theme, app shell (Dashboard, Clients, Tasks, Reports,
   Settings)
2. Seed script: IDS with the exact resources/repos above (4 separate
   DO apps, 2 Supabase projects, 2 edge function resources, 2 Vercel
   environments, 1 Expo app) and realistic mock metrics, restarts,
   health checks, deployments, builds and tasks (30 days), so the UI
   works without live integrations
3. Clients: list, create, edit, detail page
4. Provider accounts + resources UI: add account, test connection,
   discover and import resources, set environment, link repository,
   set health check URL
5. Tasks: quick-add (title, client, due date), complete, views for
   Overdue / Today / Upcoming, filter by client
6. Morning dashboard: greeting; client card with production RAG status,
   gauges per production resource, uptime, restarts, latest deploys;
   muted development section; today + overdue tasks; GitHub activity;
   "awaiting production" count; warnings
7. Client detail: tabs for Production / Development / Mobile /
   Activity. Charts (24h/7d/30d), deploy timeline, builds, repos
8. Live DigitalOcean App Platform integration
9. Live Supabase integration
10. Live Vercel integration
11. Live GitHub integration + release tracking
12. Live Expo/EAS integration + iOS store version
13. Health checks + uptime
14. Monthly reports:
    - Pick client + month -> aggregate into a data snapshot
    - Client-facing sections: service availability (uptime per
      production service), performance (avg/peak CPU and memory,
      summarised), database growth, edge function usage,
      "Released to production" (PRs/features), "On staging, awaiting
      production", deployments per environment, mobile releases
      (versions, builds, store versions), tasks completed, summary
    - Exclude internal-only data (errors, restarts, plans, connection
      issues, raw DB metrics)
    - Match the layout in docs/report-template/
    - DRAFT -> edit summary and hide/show sections -> PUBLISH
      (snapshot frozen)
    - Public read-only view at /r/[publicToken]; PDF via Puppeteer
15. AI (AI_ENABLED): morning briefing and draft report summary written
    in plain English (editable before publish)
16. Phase 2: email alerts, Google Play version, renewals calendar,
    time tracking, AWS integration, more clients

